  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1118 PM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nFriday night through Wednesday:\n\nA broad, but low amplitude upper ridge, will move into the \ncentral and srn USA this weekend and continue into next week.\nWell organized low to mid level warm, moist advection that will\nbring the ridge into the central USA will affect srn WI Sat \nafternoon into Sunday. PWATs will rise above 1.5 inches with\nconditional unstable conditions developing. Showers and\nthunderstorms are likely Sat nt when the main tropospheric\nbaroclinic zone will move across the region. However, the \nbaroclinic zone will stall early in the week with continued \nchances for showers and storms each day. Heavy rainfall may \nbecome a concern this weekend into early next week. The \nstationary front should gradually shift more south by Tue or \nWed. \n\nGehring",
